# Reduck take-home (Snapchat for Web)

## Safety (non-negotiable)
- Use a **dedicated Snapchat test account** only — never a personal account.
- Keep request rate **low**: deliberate delays between navigations and scrapes; no parallel spam runs.
- Automate only what a normal user would plausibly do. **No** mass DMs, friend spam, Story/Spotlight blasting, engagement farming.
- Prefer **read** flows. Never auto-Send messages. Do not click Send in any script.
- Acknowledge account-ban risk in `web.snapchat.com/docs/SCOPE.md` and `web.snapchat.com/docs/QA.md`.

## Scope lock
- Host: `web.snapchat.com` only (folder `web.snapchat.com/`).
- Scripts: `check_session`, `list_chats`, `open_chat`, `list_chat_messages` only.
- No unofficial Snap APIs, no mobile automation.

## Language
- **English** for code, meta, tests, rules, SCOPE, QA, README.
- **French** only for Loom narration and the final submission email.

## Working habits
- Log every notable Reduck or Snapchat friction in `web.snapchat.com/docs/QA.md` while building (not at the end).
- Discovery via `start_session` + `exec_code`; ship via draft → test → promote.
- Do not fake success if session/cookies fail — document P0 and unblock auth first.
